---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import YouTube from '../components/YouTube.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Project: LocoRoco Simple | Linus Ekberg"
  description="LocoRoco Lite, a minimalistic remake made solo in Unity for the S.U.M.M.E.R. game jam, where it placed second."
>
  <div class="project wrap">
    <Card class="solo loco">
      <div class="cols-loco">
        <div class="main">
          <h1 class="page-title">Game Jam: LocoRoco Lite</h1>
          <ul class="facts">
            <li>Solo Project</li>
            <li>Unity</li>
            <li>
              Game Jam Theme: S.U.M.M.E.R. (<strong>S</strong>implistic <strong>U</strong>ltra <strong>M</strong>ini<strong>M</strong>alistic <strong>E</strong>pic <strong>R</strong>emake.
            </li>
            <li>
              Game Jam Description: The goal of this game jam was to take a game and break it down to its core mechanics and
              remake the game in a minimalistic way.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="raleway">
            <p>
              I started off by <strong>identifying</strong> what the most <strong>essential mechanics</strong> would be for the game.
              I thought to myself: <em>What is this game's identity? What makes it fun?</em> Which led me to these core points:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Camera tilting:</strong> The player is controlled by moving tilting the camera up to ~20 degrees.</li>
              <li>
                <strong>Growing:</strong> The player should be able to find fruit that grows the player character when eating,
                which should also affect the physics of the character.
                <ul>
                  <li>Additionally, this gives the player a side goal of collecting all the fruit, which is represented on the UI.</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Playfulness:</strong> All aspects of the game should feel playful and childish. Sound design, level
                design, aesthetic, physics etc.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="finally">
              Finally, I wanted levels to be <strong>fast</strong> and <strong>easy</strong> to create, as I had very limited time
              to work on this project, but still wanted as much out of it as possible.
            </p>
          </div>
          <Figure loop="locoroco-creating-level-fast" width={442} alt="Building a LocoRoco Lite level quickly in Unity" />
        </div>
        <div class="side">
          <YouTube id="_ioWPSceqhs" title="S.U.M.M.E.R. Game Jam: LocoRoco Lite" />
          <Figure loop="locoroco-tilt" width={268} caption="Prototyping: Camera tilting" />
          <Figure loop="locoroco-eat" width={269} caption="Prototyping: Growing" />
          <Figure loop="locoroco-physics" width={273} caption="Prototyping: Playful physics" />
          <p class="raleway outro">
            This project was <strong>super fun</strong> to work on despite the fact that I didn't have a lot of time to commit to
            it! It really <strong>taught me</strong> how <strong>fast</strong> you can get a game to a <strong>playable</strong> and <strong>fun</strong> state,
            as long as you have a few fun and interesting mechanics! I ended up placing second in this game jam!
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Card>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .cols-loco {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 460px) minmax(0, 440px);
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 30px;
  }

  .main {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 26px;
    align-content: start;
    padding-left: 8px;
  }

  .main .facts {
    margin-top: 6px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .main h1 + .facts {
    margin-top: -20px;
  }

  .raleway {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #222;
  }

  .raleway strong {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #000;
  }

  .raleway ul {
    padding-left: 1.8em;
  }

  .raleway ul ul {
    list-style: circle;
  }

  .finally {
    margin-top: 2.2em;
  }

  .side {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 26px;
    align-content: start;
  }

  .side > :global(.embed) {
    width: 401px;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .outro {
    margin-top: 30px;
    margin-left: -26px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .cols-loco {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .main {
      padding-left: 0;
    }

    .outro {
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
